nav2_mppi_controller: input-delay compensation (model_delay_vx / model_delay_vy / model_delay_wz)

Backport of upstream Nav2 PR #6154 (https://github.com/ros-navigation/navigation2/pull/6154),
merged to main as commit 374cd2556640586251b1e49a346f6c8d0cb76224, ported to xtensor for
Jazzy 1.3.13 (navigation2 f4108e5b1c2bce804a1aa0c7be6673a8eb4a1501). Upstream will not backport
it to Jazzy (ABI); it ships in Lyrical, where this overlay is deleted.

Differences from upstream: the Jazzy method name MotionModel::initialize() is kept (upstream:
setConstraints()) and the delays are trailing default arguments, so every existing Jazzy call
site and test compiles unchanged; the delay shift runs per batch row inside predict() over
xt::xtensor<float, 2> instead of a separate Eigen pass. Semantics are identical: a delay is the
total actuation latency, offset = floor(delay / model_dt + 0.5), and offset 0 or 1 is a no-op.

Apply with: git apply -p1 <this file>   (from the navigation2 checkout root)

